    "result_text": "All tests pass. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required that creating an owner returns a `displayName` formatted exactly as `LastName, FirstName` from the stored names. I implemented it cleanly, placing each piece of logic where it belongs:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `displayName` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema. The DTOs are generated from this spec, so this adds `displayName` to `OwnerDto` (returned by both create and get).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Person.java`** \u2014 Added a derived `getDisplayName()` accessor returning `lastName + \", \" + firstName`. Since the first/last names live on `Person`, that's the natural home for the name-based formatting, and it's reused by every `Person` subclass rather than duplicated.\n\nMapStruct's `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto` auto-maps the source getter `getDisplayName()` to the target `displayName` field by name, so no extra mapping wiring was needed \u2014 both the create (`addOwner`) and read (`getOwner`) paths go through it.\n\nThe acceptance test (`AcceptanceTest.coreComputesDisplayName`) and the full build are green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` / `BUILD SUCCESS`).",
